Every caller handles the -1 from StartOf, StartOfNamed and PaddingAt:
- the loop placement (:3223) falls back to the offset;
- ReachedAt (:3687) and StartOfNamed (:3720) give -1;
- TryReadXRefSection (:5100) reports the guard;
- shortBy is computed only in branch (c), where hybridStart >= 0.
-1 never enters _sectionsReadAt.

The partition dependence left is the one #52 names, stated precisely. A place whose line starts before the bytes searched is dropped exactly when its read-back gives at most before + at bytes, with before = min(4,096, spanStart) and at between 1 and 1,025:
- caps of 4,097 bytes or less, and 4,096-byte block sources, drop every such place wherever spanStart is at least 4,096;
- caps from 4,098 to 5,121 drop the places more than cap - 4,097 bytes into the window;
- caps of 5,122 or more drop none.
A dropped real keyword or /Type /XRef header then reads as main reads these shapes (NotFound and xref.section-missing) where whole reads take it as found moved and Malformed. That is #52's comment; the rows a dropped real table read stay in the index, which is #320. The remark and the docs rows describe this truly.
